        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Bilaterally paired longitudinal vein; the anterior cardinal returns blood from the head, and the posterior cardinal returns it from the trunk; these two vessels join together on each side as the common cardinal vein (duct of Cuvier; misnamed the vitelline vein) that leads across the yolk cell to the heart&apos;s sinus venosus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TAO:0000186</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>duct of Cuvier</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>zebrafish_anatomy</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ZFA:0000186</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>common cardinal vein</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
