        <obo:IAO_0000115>The multi-tissue,  vagal lobe is a large, paired brain stem structure flanking the unpaired facial lobe laterally.  The vagal lobe contains motor and gustatory neurons. While some degree of histological segregation is apparent within the vagal lobe, a clear lamination, as seen in goldfish or carp is absent.</obo:IAO_0000115>
