                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ZFS_0000044"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Neural arch that extends along the dorso-lateral surface of the last preural centra and/or ural centra and the notochord (Arratia &amp; Schultze, 1992). An uroneural develops as a modification of the neural arch of an ural centrum (Patterson, 1968). The series of uroneurals may include from 7 to 1 elements that are numbered from rostral to caudal. An uroneural is a paired membrane bone.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TAO:0000602</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>uroneurals</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>zebrafish_anatomy</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>ZFA:0000602</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>uroneural</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ZFA_0000602"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Neural arch that extends along the dorso-lateral surface of the last preural centra and/or ural centra and the notochord (Arratia &amp; Schultze, 1992). An uroneural develops as a modification of the neural arch of an ural centrum (Patterson, 1968). The series of uroneurals may include from 7 to 1 elements that are numbered from rostral to caudal. An uroneural is a paired membrane bone.</owl:annotatedTarget>
