        <obo:IAO_0000115>The fourth Weberian ossicle. The tripus is a complex modification of the parapophysis and rib of the third vertebra. Anteriorly it attaches to the interosseus ligament and posteriorly it extends as a transformator process embedded in the tunica externa of the swim bladder.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TAO:0000698</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
