            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Acellular anatomical structure that is a layer of collagen fibrils in the immature integument in a subepidermal space. At first, the fibrils are all oriented in the same direction, later they form the complex plywood-like structure that is characteristic of the dermal deep region.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TAO:0001186</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>primary dermal stroma</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
