                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ZFS_0000044"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Ceratobranchial bone that is the most posterior, bilaterally paired ventral pharyngeal arch bone. Ceratobranchial 5 ossifies before ceratobranchials 1-4.  In the adult, ceratobranchial 5 is heavily ossified and crescent-shaped with two to three rows of posteromedially directed teeth. The anteroventral tips of ceratobranchials 5 meet medially and are ligamentously joined.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TAO:0001239</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>zebrafish_anatomy</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
