        <obo:IAO_0000115>The coronomeckelian is a membrane bone that ossifies on Meckel&apos;s cartilage where the tendon from the adductor mandibulae A3 inserts (6.1mm).  In the adult, the coronomeckelian is a small, irregularly shaped bone that is fused to the dorsomedial surface of the anguloarticular, just dorsal to Meckel&apos;s cartilage.</obo:IAO_0000115>
