            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The extracellular matrix between the myocardium and the endocardium. The cardiac jelly plays a central role in the septation of the heart and comprises most of the thickness of the heart wall at early stages, but disappears as the heart differentiates.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TAO:0001318</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
