            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Oocyte part of stage IV ovarian follicle. Stage IV oocytes are large and filled with noncrystalline yolky bodies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TAO:0001568</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Stage 4 oocyte</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>mature oocytes</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>oocytes stage IV</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>zebrafish_anatomy</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>postvitellogenic oocyte</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ZFA:0001568</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/zfa#cell_slim"/>
        <rdfs:comment>In stage IV (oocyte maturation), oocytes increase slightly in size, become translucent, and their yolk becomes non-crystalline as they undergo final meiotic maturation in vivo (and in response to DHP in vitro).  ZDB-PUB-961014-1020.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>oocyte stage IV</rdfs:label>
