            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Portion of tissue that gives rise to the lens. The lens of the zebrafish forms by delamination of lens placodal cells and not through invagination. This results in a solid spherical mass as opposed to a hollow lens vesicle. Detachment of the solid lens vesicle of zebrafish at 24-26 hpf is accomplished in part by apoptosis, similar to mammals.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>TAO:0002205</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym> immature lens</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>lens mass</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>lens vesicle</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>zebrafish_anatomy</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>presumptive lens</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ZFA:0001679</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Dbxref for ZFIN changed to match actual database accession number.  Old Dbxref ZDB-ANAT-090226-2 correct Dbxref ZDB-ANAT-090227-6.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>solid lens vesicle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
