            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The posterior hypaxial muscle is an early-forming ventral body wall muscle, located immediately posterior to the fin and positioned like a chest muscle. Migratory muscle precursor from somites 4-7 using the middle and posterior stream contribute to the PHM. Stabilizes the sternohyoid during suction feeding.  Insertion point is on the cleithrum.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>ceriv</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2020-07-01T11:21:03Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>inferior obliquus muscle</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>anterior hypaxial muscle </oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>ventral-most hypaxial muscle </oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>zebrafish_anatomy</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PHM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ZFA:0005926</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>posterior hypaxial muscle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
